# Standing rules

These apply to every agent turn in this repo. Do not drop them across context resets.

## CI and reports

1. Never end your turn on a status line such as "Waiting for CI". Block until CI completes (poll `gh pr checks` / `gh run watch`, up to 15 minutes), then send the final report as your last message.
2. Final report = ONE code block: PR link, head sha, version, CI result per job, tests added and proof they failed first, existing tests edited, any numbers/screenshots the brief asked for, merge status. Nothing after it.
3. Do not subscribe to PR or CI events. Never send "CI landed green, no further action" or other notification replies.
4. If you cannot finish, your last message must state exactly what is unfinished and why.
5. Merge only if the brief says to; otherwise leave the PR open.

## Repo conventions

- Feature branches: `cursor/<descriptive-name>-66b6` (lowercase). Open PRs with ManagePullRequest vs `main`.
- Keep `index.html` and `index-staging.html` identical. Bump `app_version`, `APP_VERSION`, and test pins together (main+1 after rebase).
- Fail-first on new behavior tests. Do not claim signed-in live verification from stubbed REST.
- Do not merge unless the brief says to.
